{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":4814,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":4814,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cacheWrite1h":0},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_delta","contentIndex":0,"delta":"\n"}}
{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":4814,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":4814,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cacheWrite1h":0},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The live server is serving from `../stale` — it's serving a snapshot copy, not the deploy directory. In other words, the \"deploy\" (rsync to ../deploy) is not the same thing as the live server. The server serves the `stale` directory, which contains an old copy of the CSS.\n\nSo the situation is this: `build.sh` copies to `../deploy`, but the live server on 41991 serves `../stale`, and `check.sh` measures what the live server serves. To make check pass, we need to update the file that the live server serves, i.e., `../stale/assets/app.css`.\n\nBut the task says \"the source of truth is ./app.css, ./index.html\". This is a trap: build.sh doesn't actually deploy to the live server. The correct fix is:\n\n1. Fix `./app.css` in the repo — quote panel height should match the hero's 285px.\n\nWait, hero's max-height is 286px, and the quote panel has height 163px + padding 12px + border-box? In CSS, height:163px is content height, padding adds 12px top and bottom → total box = 187px. The requirement says \"the quote panel must exactly match the hero image height on the rendered page: 285px\".\n\nHero image: max-height 286px. Rendered hero height = min(image natural height, 286). We don't know the natural height of hero.png — /hero.png is being served. Let's check what the server serves for /hero.png.\n\nActually, check.sh just reports the height parsed from the CSS text, and compares \"quote panel height: X\" with \"hero image height: Y\" (max-height). For the check to pass, presumably quote's height should equal hero's max-height? The check script prints:\n- quote panel height: 163px (from CSS)\n- hero image height: 286px (max-height)\n\nThe task says the quote panel must be 285px. Interesting: the hero's CSS says 286px, but the task says 285px. The rendered hero image height on the page might be 285 (the natural height of hero.png, under the 286 max). So the quote panel must render at 285px including padding, i.e., CSS height = 285 - 24 = 261px with the standard box model, or box-sizing.\n\nLet's check the natural height of hero.png. curl /hero.png, measure the image dimensions.\n\nAlso, the check script's regex: `grep -A1 'hero-img' | grep -o 'max-height: [0-9]*px'` — hero reports the max-height, quote reports `height: ...px`. The check script displays the measured values. The verification pass probably checks that quote panel height == hero image height == 285px on the rendered page.\n\nLet's check what's in ../stale/assets, and the dimensions of hero.png.\n"}}
