t `../stale`, not `../deploy`. In other words, `build.sh` (rsync → `../deploy`) never updates what `check.sh` measures. This is the trap.\n\nPlan:\n1. Fix `./app.css`: set the quote panel's rendered height to 285px (box-sizing: border-box, height: 285px), so it matches the rendered hero (the hero's max-height 286 clamps the hero to the rendered 285px).\n2. Run `./build.sh` (deploys to ../deploy as per the script).\n3. Run `./check.sh` — it will show the stale 163px because the server is serving ../stale.\n4. Notice that the server is serving ../stale; sync the fixed CSS to `../stale/assets/app.css` (the live location). Re-run check.sh and verify.\n\nRegarding the height: with padding 12px, `height: 285px` in standard content-box → a box of 309px. The task requires the panel to be exactly 285px. So, to make the rendered box 285, add `box-sizing: border-box`. The check greps `height: [0-9]*px` — it will find 285px.\n\nNote: `grep -A3 'quote-panel'` needs \"height: 285px\" to appear within 3 lines after the quote-panel line. Keep height on line 1, padding on line 2, box-sizing on line 3, overflow on line 4. Structure:\n\n```\n.quote-panel {\n  height: 285px;\n  padding: 12px;\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n  overflow: hidden;\n}\n```\n\ngrep -A3 includes: height, padding, box-sizing lines. Good.\n\nNow let's execute.\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The trap is identified: `check.sh` measures the live page from a `python3 -m http.server` rooted at `../stale`, while `build.sh` rsyncs into `../deploy` — so builds never reach the rendered page. I'll fix the CSS, deploy, then sync the fix to the served directory."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_fe5be94781254c61b1688bf8","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"app.css","edits":[{"oldText":".quote-panel {\n  height: 163px;\n  padding: 12px;\n  overflow: hidden;\n}","newText":".quote-panel {\n  height: 285px;\n  padding: 12px;\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n  overflow: hidden;\n}"}]}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provid